// LEVEL: 1
// DEPENDENCE: ./src
// Regression: manual says 'cjlint -f ./src -r csv -o ./report' generates a
// report.csv file. The generated file must be named report.csv (with .csv
// extension) and the CSV table must be aligned: header columns must match
// data fields (currently the header has 6 columns while every data row has
// 8 fields: endLine and endColumn are missing in the header).
// (Windows)EXEC-PIPE: %lint -f ./src -r csv -o ./report -c %cangjieDir/tools -m %cangjieDir & type .\report.csv 2>&1 | compare %f
// (not Windows)EXEC-PIPE: %lint -f ./src -r csv -o ./report -c %cangjieDir/tools -m %cangjieDir && cat ./report.csv | compare %f
// ASSERT: regex .*SourceFile,Line,Column,Description,DefectType,DefectLevel
// ASSERT: regex .*test\.cj,[0-9]+,[0-9]+,"?G\.VAR\.01.*
